# Copy to .env (make up does this when .env is missing). Values here are for the
# local Compose stack only; cloud values live in SSM. Compose reads this file for
# ${VAR} substitution and the Makefile exports it for host-side dbt and tests.
# The Makefile includes this file as make syntax, so values must not contain
# "$" or "#" and must not be quoted.

# Warehouse: the PostGIS database that dbt and the loaders write to.
# WAREHOUSE_HOST and WAREHOUSE_PORT are how the host reaches it; Compose overrides
# them for the Dagster containers, which reach it on the internal network.
# The host port is 5433 because 5432 is often taken by another local Postgres.
#
# WAREHOUSE_PASSWORD here, and MINIO_ROOT_USER and MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD below,
# are placeholders anyone can read in this repository. make up and make
# rotate-owner-password run make check-credentials first, which refuses while
# any of the three in .env is empty or equals any of these placeholders, quoted
# or padded too, so generate each in .env, without printing it, with the Git
# Bash command in the README (Credentials).
# A new WAREHOUSE_PASSWORD reaches an existing warehouse only through
# make rotate-owner-password; the README gives the order of the steps.
WAREHOUSE_HOST=localhost
WAREHOUSE_PORT=5433
WAREHOUSE_USER=mesh
WAREHOUSE_PASSWORD=mesh
WAREHOUSE_DB=mesh_terrain

# The role the tests and the development dbt builds (make check, make
# dbt-build) connect as: no privilege on raw, raw_dev_wh or raw_dev_ta, so any
# write a test sends there fails (docker/warehouse/test-role.sql). make check
# and make dbt-build create or update it in the running warehouse first, and
# make up does once both values are set. It must differ
# from WAREHOUSE_USER, the owner, which make dbt-build-real, the loaders and
# Dagster use. While it is unset no test connects as the owner; a warehouse
# that refuses the login fails the warehouse tests.
#
# Only the main checkout's .env sets the two, without the leading "# " and with
# real values (Casey, PR #74). A worktree's .env, copied from this file, sets
# neither; a check there gets them from the shell, which exports only those
# two lines of the main checkout's .env, joined with && to the make command in
# one Git Bash command, since an export is gone once its shell ends and each
# agent tool call is a new shell (README, Test role). For example:
#   while IFS= read -r line; do export "$line"; done < <(grep -E '^WAREHOUSE_TEST_(USER|PASSWORD)=' /c/Users/Casey/Desktop/GEO/mesh-terrain/.env | tr -d '\r') && make check DBT_DEV_TARGET=dev_ta
# A value from the shell wins over a .env that sets one. make check, make
# dbt-build and make test-role stop without them. The export line, make and
# test-role.sql print neither value; the role's name can still reach the
# server log when a login is refused (README, Test role, lists every case),
# and pytest scrubs only its test reports, collection reports and warnings
# summary, so never run warehouse tests with -s, --capture=no,
# --capture=tee-sys, --pdb, --trace or --full-trace, and note that an
# INTERNALERROR prints arguments, and locals with -l. Pick a distinctive role
# name of eight characters or more.
# WAREHOUSE_TEST_USER=<test role name>
# WAREHOUSE_TEST_PASSWORD=<test role password>

# Dagster run, event and schedule storage. Same Postgres server, separate database,
# so a warehouse reset never loses run history and a Dagster upgrade never touches
# the warehouse.
DAGSTER_PG_DB=dagster

# Object store standing in for S3. S3_ENDPOINT_URL is the API; the console is on
# MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT. The Dagster containers get the internal endpoint from Compose.
# MINIO_ROOT_USER and MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD are placeholders to replace, as above;
# MinIO reads them every time it starts.
MINIO_ROOT_USER=minio
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=minio12345
MINIO_API_PORT=9000
MINIO_CONSOLE_PORT=9001
S3_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:9000
RAW_BUCKET=mesh-terrain-raw

# Dagster webserver host port.
DAGSTER_PORT=3000

# "console" for a developer terminal, "json" in containers (Compose sets json).
LOG_FORMAT=console

# Host folder that holds snapshot folders (ADR 0005), outside every Docker volume.
# Compose mounts it read-only at /snapshots in the Dagster containers and sets
# SNAPSHOTS_DIR=/snapshots there; SNAPSHOTS_DIR here is what the host commands
# (make load, make capture, the reduction) read. CI mounts an empty folder instead.
SNAPSHOTS_HOST_DIR=C:/Users/Casey/mesh-terrain-data/snapshots
SNAPSHOTS_DIR=C:/Users/Casey/mesh-terrain-data/snapshots

# Host folder that receives engine runs, one <run-id>/ folder each, outside every
# Docker volume and never in git. A run writes <run-id>.partial/ and renames it
# once its manifest is written; nothing deletes a run folder automatically
# (Casey, PR #27, 2026-11-15). Nothing mounts it yet; make engine will.
RUNS_HOST_DIR=C:/Users/Casey/mesh-terrain-data/runs

# Secret: 32 random bytes written as 64 hex characters; no default, never logged
# (ADR 0005 item 3). Only the capture and reduction read it, from this file
# through their settings; the Makefile does not export it and no container gets it.
NODE_ID_HMAC_KEY=

# Optional. Where the dbt project lives when it is not <repo>/dbt.
# DBT_PROJECT_DIR=

# Optional. The dbt development target make check and make dbt-build build on,
# one per track so two runs at once never share schemas (dbt/README.md,
# Targets): dev_wh, the default, for Track B, or dev_ta for Track A. make
# refuses any other value before any recipe runs, prod and an empty
# DBT_DEV_TARGET= included, so the line stays commented out or names one of
# the two.
# DBT_DEV_TARGET=dev_wh

# Optional. The NTIA ITM shared library that terrain/itm.py loads (ADR 0002).
# The Dagster image builds it at this path; set it only for a host-side build.
# ITM_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib/libitm.so

# Optional, Windows hosts whose antivirus re-signs HTTPS: a CA bundle that
# includes the scanner's root, so Python can reach PyPI and the dbt hub
# (README, "Running on Windows").
# SSL_CERT_FILE=C:/Users/you/.certs/ca-bundle.pem
# REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE=C:/Users/you/.certs/ca-bundle.pem

# Optional, the same hosts: the same bundle for the warehouse and Dagster
# image builds. They reach it only as a BuildKit secret mounted for the steps
# that download over HTTPS (PyPI, the dbt hub, github.com and the PostgreSQL
# apt archive), so it never lands in an image (docker/compose.ca-bundle.yml).
# make pdal also mounts it read-only into the PDAL container, which reads
# USGS lidar over HTTPS while it runs.
# Leave empty when the build reaches those hosts directly, as in CI.
# Example: C:/Users/you/.certs/ca-bundle.pem
CA_BUNDLE_PATH=
